# Last-in-chapter floats stay with the citing text

## Symptom

The citing subsection ends a page with leftover whitespace. The next folio is only the figure, vertically centred. The following `\chapter` (or `\section`) starts one page later.

## Cause

`[ht]` cannot fit the diagram plus caption in the leftover. `\chapter` issues `\clearpage`, and `[section]{placeins}` does the same at `\section`. The pending float is shipped onto its own float page. A short diagram still gets that page, because `\clearpage` flushes it rather than waiting for `\floatpagefraction`.

## Fix

Local enlarge plus here-placement, sized to the shortfall, then rebuild and look at the folio. One site in `Thesis_v5.tex` still uses it:

| Figure | Enlarge | What flushed it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `fig:ffiseam` | `52pt` (14 Sep 2026) | `\chapter{Discussion}` |

`fig:ngran` does not use this fix. A `64pt` enlarge put the caption in the bottom margin, and a shorter stack was rejected. A `\clearpage` before the figure sends it to the next page at full size, and the following section continues under it. Do not put the enlarge back and do not shrink the diagram.

```latex
% leftover is short of the diagram plus caption, so [ht] defers it
\enlargethispage{52pt}
\begin{figure}[!ht]
```

Confirm: heading, citing paragraph, and figure share one folio. Caption not clipped. No Overfull `\vbox`. Page numbers live in the header in this class, so a modest bottom enlarge is safe.

## Do not

- `[H]` as the first try. That is a per-table lever in `AGENT.md` and strands short pages when the float still does not fit.
- `\newpage` before the subsection. The hole moves to the page before.
- Shrink every figure to `0.62\linewidth`. Measured, saves 0 pages.
- Drop the caption's measured numbers to save lines. Those macros stay.
